1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
Togashi!

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:08,260
You guys need something?

3
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:11,560
We just got word of your fight with Takashima.

4
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:12,380
Yeah.

5
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:15,920
He should know better than to play his little tough guy games with me.

6
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:18,300
But he's an idiot and went for it anyway.

7
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:20,580
So I sent him straight and put an end to that.

8
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:27,760
By the way, if you haven't realized it yet, this mess is all their fault.

9
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:28,860
Their fault?

10
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:29,480
Who?

11
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:31,420
Do you mean the promoted players?

12
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:34,700
Togashi, what the heck happened between you guys?

13
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:39,680
You'll find out soon enough, no doubt.

14
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:37,131
Okay, listen up. We have three new members, at least for the next week or so. Consider this a trial period. I'm counting on you to help them if they need it. If all goes well and they prove to be skilled, they'll be invited to join Esperion Jr. next year. Your guidance is a pre-

15
00:02:37,131 --> 00:02:48,211
Let me introduce myself. The name is Keiji Togashi. I'm a forward, and I plan on going pro someday. If you guys are some half-ass lazy team, you can forget about recruiting me!

16
00:02:49,331 --> 00:02:55,291
What? Seriously? Togashi was invited here as a trialist when he was in the sixth grade?

17
00:02:56,211 --> 00:02:57,491
Yeah, sure was.

18
00:03:00,111 --> 00:03:04,191
Anyway, who cares? It doesn't matter. What are you doing in my room, creeps?

19
00:03:04,331 --> 00:03:06,091
Uh, it's my room too, numbnuts.

20
00:03:06,091 --> 00:03:14,071
I got demoted from the A-team, okay? After just one month, I wasn't good at anything. It's humiliating. Now get out of here!

21
00:03:18,631 --> 00:03:23,331
What's up with you, Tachibana? You said you wanted to talk, but it sounds like you're looking for drama.

22
00:03:24,451 --> 00:03:29,671
You want the tea on Togashi and Kurata's crew? Kind of weird, because I don't think you ever really talked to me.

23
00:03:29,671 --> 00:03:43,051
Yuma, listen. I've made up my mind. Whatever it takes, we need to crush Musashino. No more doubts. I'm in this for the team. One hundred percent.

24
00:03:43,051 --> 00:03:50,751
You should see the look on your face right now. Way to brood.

25
00:03:50,751 --> 00:04:01,371
I don't usually invest in other people's problems. But what the hell. There's a popular saying in soccer, you know? It's kind of a sad generalization.

26
00:04:02,511 --> 00:04:04,691
Youth players are mentally weak.

27
00:04:04,691 --> 00:04:12,531
Not bad at all for a baby trainee.

28
00:04:12,951 --> 00:04:14,331
Well, yeah, of course I'm not.

29
00:04:15,291 --> 00:04:17,031
This is their basic training?

30
00:04:17,471 --> 00:04:19,351
What they do every single day?

31
00:04:19,351 --> 00:04:24,691
And act like it's nothing. So this is what a J-League team's academy is like.

32
00:04:24,891 --> 00:04:25,931
Yo, Togashi.

33
00:04:27,111 --> 00:04:28,271
Um, yes, sir.

34
00:04:28,911 --> 00:04:33,811
I'm seeing quite a bit of improvement. Does that mean you've been practicing since last time?

35
00:04:34,491 --> 00:04:40,871
You bet I have. I kept replaying what you taught me back then in my head, and then I kept practicing it. Over and over again.

36
00:04:40,991 --> 00:04:41,871
Way to go, kid.

37
00:04:43,151 --> 00:04:47,931
Tatsuya Fukuda. The guy who gave me advice when I met him at the National Center last year.

38
00:04:49,351 --> 00:04:56,471
But come on, man. I finally get a chance to join the junior youth team, and now everyone's saying next year you're gonna coach youth.

39
00:04:58,271 --> 00:05:01,991
I'm sure we'll work together one day. If you're lucky.

40
00:05:04,411 --> 00:05:08,951
I'm so jealous of you, getting to talk to Coach Fukuda one-on-one like that.

41
00:05:11,091 --> 00:05:13,191
Yeah, so? What the hell do you want?

42
00:05:14,031 --> 00:05:18,731
That's funny. You actually do talk like a real punk. Nice to meet you. I'm Kuroda.

43
00:05:19,351 --> 00:05:25,231
Huh. Other than Squinty, you're the only one who said two words to me. None of the others even tried.

44
00:05:26,191 --> 00:05:29,391
Are all the players in this academy shy and quiet, or what?

45
00:05:30,171 --> 00:05:32,831
I think it's just the way you talk to them at first.

46
00:05:33,431 --> 00:05:36,911
What about these guys? No one talks to them, so it's not just me.

47
00:05:36,911 --> 00:05:43,111
Well, everyone here is very focused on going pro, so we don't spend a lot of time socializing with each other.

48
00:05:43,111 --> 00:05:52,431
You were amazing out there today, though. I mean, you managed to keep up with our training session. You've got a strong build and good technique.

49
00:05:52,431 --> 00:05:58,451
So listen, we have a practice match with a local elementary school team this afternoon.

50
00:05:58,891 --> 00:06:03,751
Wait, back up! So you're saying there's a game? That's incredible! Yes!

51
00:06:03,751 --> 00:06:07,471
Before we go, why don't we try some stealth out on the field?

52
00:06:07,851 --> 00:06:08,711
What do you mean?

53
00:06:09,391 --> 00:06:16,891
Your height. We should make better use of it. You could try knocking the ball down in front of the goal, and then I could run onto it.

54
00:06:17,671 --> 00:06:21,751
If that leads to a goal, it would be a great way to showcase your skills.

55
00:06:21,751 --> 00:06:35,811
Awesome. There's fastened in actual games. They are in training.

56
00:06:41,811 --> 00:06:50,451
If I join this team, I'll get to play at this level every day. It'll definitely help me reach my goal to go pro.

57
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:52,651
I couldn't have asked for a better shot.

58
00:06:53,671 --> 00:06:57,591
You could try knocking the ball down in front of the goal to showcase your skills.

59
00:06:58,011 --> 00:07:03,811
I don't like being made to provide assists, but if it means I can show off a bit, I'm all for it.

60
00:07:04,071 --> 00:07:06,051
Stay there, Trilus! Don't move!

61
00:07:07,551 --> 00:07:08,791
All right, go ahead!

62
00:07:09,791 --> 00:07:11,271
Number six, go get in the middle!

63
00:07:11,531 --> 00:07:11,931
Right!

64
00:07:13,371 --> 00:07:18,551
Something that keeps bugging me, though, is it feels like they play differently with each other than they do with us,

65
00:07:18,551 --> 00:07:20,131
who they're supposed to be training.

66
00:07:20,451 --> 00:07:24,211
You're using different passes, and giving different instructions!

67
00:07:25,671 --> 00:07:27,911
Sending a long ball your way, number six!

68
00:07:31,511 --> 00:07:34,851
Time to show what I can do. You better get on the end of it, dude!

69
00:07:38,151 --> 00:07:38,671
All right!

70
00:07:39,131 --> 00:07:41,931
It's a one-on-one. Time to go and bury it!

71
00:07:41,931 --> 00:07:51,731
What are you doing out there, noob? You had it!

72
00:07:52,391 --> 00:07:52,851
Yeah.

73
00:07:53,251 --> 00:07:54,291
What are you doing?

74
00:07:54,611 --> 00:07:55,931
That shot was so easy.

75
00:07:56,111 --> 00:07:57,471
You totally could have taken it.

76
00:07:58,071 --> 00:07:59,871
Are you really asking me that?

77
00:08:00,871 --> 00:08:02,811
Why didn't you do what you said you would?

78
00:08:03,351 --> 00:08:03,971
The plan.

79
00:08:03,971 --> 00:08:05,851
Huh?

80
00:08:08,311 --> 00:08:09,931
Takashima, you were so cool out there!

81
00:08:09,931 --> 00:08:11,071
Oh, hey, that's enough!

82
00:08:11,331 --> 00:08:11,711
Well!

83
00:08:12,771 --> 00:08:15,511
You invited your girlfriends to a practice match?

84
00:08:16,311 --> 00:08:17,511
Um, who's this?

85
00:08:17,711 --> 00:08:20,551
Uh, oh, he's a trialist.

86
00:08:21,411 --> 00:08:23,031
No, neither of them are my girlfriend.

87
00:08:23,031 --> 00:08:27,371
I just told them they could come along today if they felt like watching, and they did.

88
00:08:28,331 --> 00:08:31,351
Takashima's really good at soccer, so it's always fun to see him play.

89
00:08:34,051 --> 00:08:36,131
What's that face for? It's no big deal.

90
00:08:36,451 --> 00:08:38,731
Really, we're having fun. I'm staying focused.

91
00:08:39,411 --> 00:08:41,871
I keep soccer and my private life separate.

92
00:08:42,431 --> 00:08:43,731
It could be worse, you know.

93
00:08:44,091 --> 00:08:47,311
I could miss a chance to shoot while I'm in acres of space.

94
00:08:47,311 --> 00:08:54,411
Asperion Jr. These guys are the top grade school players in Tokyo.

95
00:08:55,411 --> 00:09:00,031
Everyone on the team has crazy skills, and their strength in matches feels impossible.

96
00:09:01,031 --> 00:09:04,371
They all stay focused. None of them ever let their guard down.

97
00:09:05,311 --> 00:09:09,211
So then why? Why am I so irritated by them?

98
00:09:11,791 --> 00:09:12,691
You're leaving?

99
00:09:13,251 --> 00:09:15,491
Yeah, they're on another level than us.

100
00:09:15,491 --> 00:09:18,611
What? So? That's not a surprise. You knew they would be good.

101
00:09:18,951 --> 00:09:20,791
If it was skill, we could work on it.

102
00:09:21,291 --> 00:09:21,891
It's not.

103
00:09:22,851 --> 00:09:23,751
It's them.

104
00:09:23,971 --> 00:09:25,011
They're all so scary.

105
00:09:25,411 --> 00:09:26,871
It's just not a good vibe overall.

106
00:09:29,051 --> 00:09:32,891
Whenever they're around, it's like they don't even see us in front of them.

107
00:09:33,431 --> 00:09:34,951
Makes me feel worthless, you know?

108
00:09:35,151 --> 00:09:36,331
Yeah, well, so what?

109
00:09:36,451 --> 00:09:38,051
Who cares if they look down on us?

110
00:09:38,171 --> 00:09:39,771
They don't even look down on us.

111
00:09:40,171 --> 00:09:41,371
They just...

112
00:09:41,371 --> 00:09:43,151
They don't look at us. Period.

113
00:09:43,151 --> 00:09:46,011
Didn't you feel like something was off during the game today?

114
00:09:46,331 --> 00:09:48,891
I really don't know how else to explain it, but it was.

115
00:09:50,331 --> 00:09:53,551
It felt like we were just there to use as tools for their training purposes.

116
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:56,891
I see now.

117
00:09:57,371 --> 00:10:01,011
The reason something fell off is because none of them saw me as their equal.

118
00:10:01,431 --> 00:10:03,851
I was just part of their stupid obstacle course.

119
00:10:04,611 --> 00:10:07,111
You could try knocking the ball down in front of the goal.

120
00:10:09,611 --> 00:10:13,451
And man, the scariest part is that I don't think they're doing it to be mean.

121
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:14,611
It's really freaky.

122
00:10:14,931 --> 00:10:15,551
They're doing it unconsciously.

123
00:10:16,511 --> 00:10:16,931
Huh?

124
00:10:17,391 --> 00:10:18,991
Take care, Tokushi. Best of luck.

125
00:10:18,991 --> 00:10:25,331
None of you got anything to say?

126
00:10:26,331 --> 00:10:27,871
What do you think we should say?

127
00:10:28,991 --> 00:10:31,071
Besides, you're staying, aren't you?

128
00:10:31,811 --> 00:10:33,491
We'll just continue on without them.

129
00:10:35,991 --> 00:10:38,311
By the way,

130
00:10:38,711 --> 00:10:40,251
the reason I didn't shoot

131
00:10:40,251 --> 00:10:42,291
was because I assessed the situation

132
00:10:42,291 --> 00:10:44,651
and saw that you had a better chance of scoring.

133
00:10:44,651 --> 00:10:47,411
Any more questions?

134
00:10:48,031 --> 00:10:49,411
Do you just not like scoring?

135
00:10:49,951 --> 00:10:51,531
That's the whole point of soccer!

136
00:10:51,751 --> 00:10:53,491
That's the part everyone wants to do!

137
00:10:56,531 --> 00:10:59,831
Well, if my overall goal tally helps me to become a pro, then sure.

138
00:11:00,491 --> 00:11:03,171
But today was simply just another practice game.

139
00:11:03,571 --> 00:11:04,811
So it didn't even count.

140
00:11:06,411 --> 00:11:08,611
Got some advice for you, trialist.

141
00:11:08,831 --> 00:11:11,311
You should wait until after you score to talk like that.

142
00:11:12,371 --> 00:11:14,091
That play today was a mess!

143
00:11:14,091 --> 00:11:15,811
All you have to do is kick it!

144
00:11:16,171 --> 00:11:18,651
You fail as a forward if you can't even do that!

145
00:11:18,911 --> 00:11:21,291
Who gets right up to the goal and then kicks it back?

146
00:11:21,671 --> 00:11:22,931
The whole point is to score

147
00:11:22,931 --> 00:11:24,311
and you had it all the way up there!

148
00:11:24,311 --> 00:11:34,271
I suppose the answer is we're not like you.

149
00:11:34,271 --> 00:11:51,291
I don't like this!

150
00:11:51,291 --> 00:11:53,511
What's so different about us, huh?

151
00:11:53,951 --> 00:11:55,311
Number 15, pass!

152
00:11:56,111 --> 00:11:57,871
I can't think about that now.

153
00:11:58,251 --> 00:11:59,511
If I want to join the team,

154
00:11:59,771 --> 00:12:01,431
I've got to make those points happen!

155
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:02,291
Return!

156
00:12:03,091 --> 00:12:05,051
Are they using me as their trial horse?

157
00:12:05,311 --> 00:12:05,771
Fine.

158
00:12:06,171 --> 00:12:06,531
Whatever.

159
00:12:06,931 --> 00:12:08,891
This game is survival of the fittest.

160
00:12:09,171 --> 00:12:10,151
Send it back!

161
00:12:10,731 --> 00:12:12,091
I don't care what they do.

162
00:12:12,371 --> 00:12:13,891
I'll continue to climb higher.

163
00:12:13,891 --> 00:12:17,151
Togashi, the wing!

164
00:12:17,311 --> 00:12:18,491
Play the ball out in front!

165
00:12:23,171 --> 00:12:23,691
Yeah!

166
00:12:24,011 --> 00:12:25,211
Nice leaker play, guys!

167
00:12:25,271 --> 00:12:25,811
Very good!

168
00:12:25,811 --> 00:12:30,791
Something's different today.

169
00:12:31,131 --> 00:12:33,831
It doesn't feel like they're using me as practice for some reason.

170
00:12:34,831 --> 00:12:35,451
All right.

171
00:12:35,911 --> 00:12:37,611
This way I don't gotta hold back.

172
00:12:37,971 --> 00:12:38,611
Hey, defense!

173
00:12:38,851 --> 00:12:39,351
Let's go!

174
00:12:39,471 --> 00:12:40,331
Come up through the middle!

175
00:12:42,331 --> 00:12:43,971
What is wrong with that guy?

176
00:12:44,311 --> 00:12:46,791
In the last game, he had zero problems going upfield.

177
00:12:47,171 --> 00:12:48,431
Even though he's a center back.

178
00:12:51,091 --> 00:12:52,511
What the hell is he looking at?

179
00:12:53,131 --> 00:12:54,151
That's so weird.

180
00:12:54,151 --> 00:12:56,291
They're not looking at the other team at all today.

181
00:12:57,171 --> 00:12:58,811
So what are they looking at?

182
00:13:05,871 --> 00:13:06,311
Yeah!

183
00:13:07,031 --> 00:13:07,471
Chump!

184
00:13:09,451 --> 00:13:10,311
Hey, Chump.

185
00:13:10,551 --> 00:13:11,251
What's up?

186
00:13:11,411 --> 00:13:12,831
So you can't shoot for yourself.

187
00:13:13,391 --> 00:13:13,731
Jeez.

188
00:13:14,151 --> 00:13:14,731
What now?

189
00:13:15,111 --> 00:13:16,371
You still have a problem with me?

190
00:13:16,811 --> 00:13:19,531
I want to know why all of you have been glancing over at that guy.

191
00:13:20,011 --> 00:13:21,551
He wasn't here last game.

192
00:13:21,891 --> 00:13:23,831
Isn't he the manager of the junior youth team?

193
00:13:24,951 --> 00:13:27,891
Some bigwig is here, so now you're gonna change the way you play?

194
00:13:28,051 --> 00:13:29,251
Is that what's different today?

195
00:13:29,391 --> 00:13:30,091
Huh, Chump?

196
00:13:32,051 --> 00:13:33,471
What's going on, you guys?

197
00:13:33,991 --> 00:13:35,391
Your guess is as good as mine.

198
00:13:35,611 --> 00:13:36,171
Hey, Red.

199
00:13:36,231 --> 00:13:37,031
What's your deal?

200
00:13:37,391 --> 00:13:39,291
Why didn't you push the defensive lineup?

201
00:13:39,971 --> 00:13:42,431
What's the point of staying in your own half when we're attacking?

202
00:13:42,731 --> 00:13:44,591
We've got to get goals to stay in the lead.

203
00:13:44,671 --> 00:13:45,951
That's how it works, moron!

204
00:13:47,351 --> 00:13:49,531
Hey, this is as far as we can push up.

205
00:13:49,751 --> 00:13:52,011
We still have to watch out for counterattacks.

206
00:13:52,571 --> 00:13:55,691
If a long ball were to go through to their forward, we'd lose the game.

207
00:13:55,891 --> 00:13:57,491
And I can't be having that, you know?

208
00:13:57,951 --> 00:13:59,831
Soccer's not all about scoring, Togashi.

209
00:14:00,291 --> 00:14:02,071
Don't give me that crap, Chump.

210
00:14:02,271 --> 00:14:04,771
I saw you racing upfield in the last match.

211
00:14:04,991 --> 00:14:06,131
You don't fool me, Red.

212
00:14:06,631 --> 00:14:10,591
You decided not to move up this time because the manager of the junior youth team's here.

213
00:14:11,191 --> 00:14:12,251
Tell me I'm wrong.

214
00:14:12,251 --> 00:14:15,111
Okay, you're dead wrong.

215
00:14:15,471 --> 00:14:17,891
Anyway, I'm focusing on playing defense.

216
00:14:18,251 --> 00:14:19,331
That's how I go pro.

217
00:14:19,771 --> 00:14:23,551
Unfortunately for you, we're already past that scoring-is-so-fun mindset.

218
00:14:24,131 --> 00:14:24,691
Grow up!

219
00:14:25,151 --> 00:14:28,471
The reason I shot today was because I saw that I had a better chance of scoring.

220
00:14:28,871 --> 00:14:29,951
Nothing more to it.

221
00:14:30,711 --> 00:14:32,331
So that's all you care about?

222
00:14:32,591 --> 00:14:35,071
You're playing soccer for the chance to go pro, that's it?

223
00:14:36,731 --> 00:14:38,331
What other reason is there?

224
00:14:39,291 --> 00:14:41,211
You don't like the thrill of winning?

225
00:14:42,251 --> 00:14:47,291
Hey, what are those boys fighting about over there?

226
00:14:47,591 --> 00:14:48,831
I have no idea.

227
00:14:52,351 --> 00:14:54,311
We're all giving everything we've got.

228
00:14:54,951 --> 00:14:56,211
None of us are slacking off.

229
00:14:56,751 --> 00:14:57,691
So what the heck?

230
00:14:58,551 --> 00:14:59,631
What's his dumb problem?

231
00:15:00,291 --> 00:15:02,571
Hey guys, don't be so quick to rush upfield!

232
00:15:03,491 --> 00:15:05,031
Of course we're playing to win.

233
00:15:05,031 --> 00:15:05,911
What does he think?

234
00:15:06,291 --> 00:15:08,751
I'll tighten up the defensive line and make sure of it.

235
00:15:09,111 --> 00:15:09,991
We have to win.

236
00:15:10,411 --> 00:15:11,531
Especially today.

237
00:15:12,251 --> 00:15:20,951
What the crap?

238
00:15:26,591 --> 00:15:27,151
Yes!

239
00:15:27,151 --> 00:15:34,731
Three players are going for it, including the goalie.

240
00:15:35,111 --> 00:15:35,891
That's not good.

241
00:15:36,351 --> 00:15:39,391
I might be able to clear it, but I'll also crash into the goalpost!

242
00:15:40,351 --> 00:15:41,291
Or a teammate!

243
00:15:47,411 --> 00:15:47,851
Whoa!

244
00:15:47,991 --> 00:15:49,171
Nice cover, Tokushi!

245
00:15:49,171 --> 00:15:50,211
Hey!

246
00:15:50,211 --> 00:15:51,431
Are you okay over there?

247
00:15:52,211 --> 00:15:53,211
Don't get injured.

248
00:15:53,711 --> 00:15:54,531
Become a pro.

249
00:15:55,091 --> 00:15:55,411
Win!

250
00:15:56,471 --> 00:15:58,971
Here at this academy, those are your priorities.

251
00:15:59,211 --> 00:16:00,131
In that order.

252
00:16:00,131 --> 00:16:05,351
And because that's the way you see things, you're always calculating too much and holding back.

253
00:16:06,091 --> 00:16:08,911
What the heck are you talking about, weirdo?

254
00:16:08,911 --> 00:16:11,911
Do you want to know what the worst part is?

255
00:16:13,411 --> 00:16:15,751
You guys don't even know that you're doing it.

256
00:16:15,751 --> 00:16:19,911
You've got no clue what your weaknesses are.

257
00:16:19,911 --> 00:16:23,151
So when a do-or-die match comes along, you'll be useless.

258
00:16:23,751 --> 00:16:26,011
You'll have no idea what to look out for.

259
00:16:26,011 --> 00:16:28,871
So what's considered a do-or-die match to you?

260
00:16:30,411 --> 00:16:31,011
Listen.

261
00:16:31,671 --> 00:16:34,251
We're prioritizing becoming professional soccer players.

262
00:16:34,571 --> 00:16:35,391
What's wrong with that?

263
00:16:36,671 --> 00:16:42,511
Speaking for myself, if I can't go pro, then my purpose in life will be completely destroyed.

264
00:16:43,411 --> 00:16:47,611
I'm always very aware of how I spend my time, the matches, and training.

265
00:16:49,291 --> 00:16:51,391
I'm gambling my life on this goal.

266
00:16:52,811 --> 00:16:54,571
It's everything I have.

267
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:55,971
Get it yet?

268
00:16:56,391 --> 00:16:58,171
Our stakes are much higher than yours.

269
00:16:59,671 --> 00:17:02,231
All of you are betting your lives on this way of playing?

270
00:17:02,351 --> 00:17:03,291
Talk about stupid.

271
00:17:04,411 --> 00:17:05,611
What did you say?

272
00:17:10,771 --> 00:17:16,611
I can see both sides of it, actually.

273
00:17:17,151 --> 00:17:18,671
It gives me a lot to think about.

274
00:17:20,011 --> 00:17:22,031
I mean, I do feel bad for Togashi,

275
00:17:22,551 --> 00:17:25,431
but I think Kurita made some very valid points, too.

276
00:17:25,931 --> 00:17:26,751
Yeah, same here.

277
00:17:27,411 --> 00:17:29,211
The whole idea is to go pro.

278
00:17:29,651 --> 00:17:33,431
You gotta look at the big picture and make moves that are gonna get you to your end goal.

279
00:17:33,931 --> 00:17:35,711
I was thinking of Musashino.

280
00:17:36,511 --> 00:17:38,411
Their strength today was like Togashi's.

281
00:17:38,411 --> 00:17:40,571
It's not about being right or wrong.

282
00:17:40,571 --> 00:17:44,631
It's about being strong, no matter what.

283
00:17:44,631 --> 00:17:45,631
I choose Togashi.

284
00:17:45,631 --> 00:17:46,851
I choose Togashi.

285
00:17:46,851 --> 00:17:58,151
Please stop that!

286
00:17:58,651 --> 00:17:59,811
Enough already, dude.

287
00:17:59,911 --> 00:18:00,371
Get off!

288
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:04,571
If you hate the way we play soccer so much, why'd you join our team?

289
00:18:04,711 --> 00:18:07,551
I came because I wanted to learn from manager Fukuda.

290
00:18:07,911 --> 00:18:08,411
Got it.

291
00:18:08,571 --> 00:18:09,691
Nothing to do with you.

292
00:18:10,351 --> 00:18:13,691
Hey, you know, you're the only one who hasn't changed since sixth grade.

293
00:18:13,691 --> 00:18:17,971
You're stuck in time at 11 years old, and you don't even realize it.

294
00:18:18,611 --> 00:18:22,131
You've never stopped playing those academy soccer games.

295
00:18:22,131 --> 00:18:36,411
Training's finally over.

296
00:18:36,851 --> 00:18:41,431
I know we're prepping to play Musashino, but the same drills over and over is super rough.

297
00:18:41,971 --> 00:18:46,691
I understand what Coach Nozomi's going for, but this tactic won't work if you don't already

298
00:18:46,691 --> 00:18:47,731
have good ball skills.

299
00:18:47,731 --> 00:18:51,971
So, do you think you and all the tryout guys are going to be able to pay-

300
00:18:51,971 --> 00:18:53,211
What are you implying?

301
00:18:54,411 --> 00:18:55,351
Especially him.

302
00:18:58,291 --> 00:19:01,071
So, uh, they don't seem to be in a great mood.

303
00:19:01,931 --> 00:19:02,851
It's understandable.

304
00:19:03,411 --> 00:19:05,251
They're about to play against Musashino.

305
00:19:06,351 --> 00:19:07,111
Damn it!

306
00:19:07,951 --> 00:19:10,331
Everyone on the team is in a crap-fest mood!

307
00:19:10,811 --> 00:19:13,851
I have to do something to bring them out of it so that we can work together!

308
00:19:13,851 --> 00:19:19,751
But how am I going to do that when I've got to memorize Nozomi's super-tight team tactic?

309
00:19:20,071 --> 00:19:21,371
Oh, this sucks so bad!

310
00:19:21,871 --> 00:19:24,531
I don't even know what I could do to make this team work together.

311
00:19:24,931 --> 00:19:26,071
Not like I can force them.

312
00:19:27,071 --> 00:19:28,271
But I can't give up.

313
00:19:28,731 --> 00:19:31,291
I have to say something that'll motivate them.

314
00:19:33,691 --> 00:19:34,091
Hey!

315
00:19:34,811 --> 00:19:35,971
Do you guys want to go on a picnic?

316
00:19:35,971 --> 00:19:36,751
Do you want a stay-legged train?

317
00:19:36,751 --> 00:19:41,611
Coach Nozomi's got a plan.

318
00:19:41,771 --> 00:19:44,071
But it can only be mastered through repetition.

319
00:19:45,291 --> 00:19:46,891
Regular training's not enough.

320
00:19:47,371 --> 00:19:48,751
We all have to practice it.

321
00:19:50,971 --> 00:19:51,491
Kuroda!

322
00:19:52,471 --> 00:19:54,031
You're overworking yourself.

323
00:19:56,291 --> 00:19:57,771
Is this because you're a starter?

324
00:19:58,551 --> 00:19:59,431
Very interesting.

325
00:20:00,431 --> 00:20:02,911
I know that Musashino is your old team and all.

326
00:20:03,571 --> 00:20:06,951
But I haven't seen you do anything of note in the other league games.

327
00:20:08,871 --> 00:20:09,871
Yeah, you're right.

328
00:20:10,711 --> 00:20:12,631
To be honest, I'm scared.

329
00:20:13,291 --> 00:20:14,651
I haven't slept much.

330
00:20:15,051 --> 00:20:16,491
Not since the lineup was announced.

331
00:20:17,271 --> 00:20:22,671
I'm afraid I'll play pathetically bad in front of all my old teammates and just screw it all up.

332
00:20:23,111 --> 00:20:25,791
Hey, uh, you know you're saying this out loud, right?

333
00:20:26,151 --> 00:20:26,751
Yeah, so?

334
00:20:27,471 --> 00:20:28,751
It's just how I am.

335
00:20:28,751 --> 00:20:31,291
That's just me.

336
00:20:32,051 --> 00:20:33,031
I might be weak.

337
00:20:33,611 --> 00:20:35,911
But I'm choosing not to run away this time.

338
00:20:36,311 --> 00:20:37,691
Because I want to beat them.

339
00:20:38,291 --> 00:20:40,131
Live up to Coach Nozomi's expectations.

340
00:20:40,891 --> 00:20:42,411
But I can't do it alone.

341
00:20:43,111 --> 00:20:44,271
So please, help me!

342
00:20:45,131 --> 00:20:45,771
You're wrong.

343
00:20:46,111 --> 00:20:47,091
You are not weak.

344
00:20:48,551 --> 00:20:53,111
The ones who are weak are the ones who can't talk about weakness out loud.

345
00:20:53,751 --> 00:20:54,271
Takashima?

346
00:20:55,211 --> 00:20:57,551
You guys don't even know that you're doing it.

347
00:20:58,751 --> 00:21:01,271
I'll tell you the truth.

348
00:21:02,051 --> 00:21:02,571
Tachibana.

349
00:21:02,911 --> 00:21:03,211
Aoi.

350
00:21:03,831 --> 00:21:05,191
You may have heard this by now.

351
00:21:05,611 --> 00:21:06,751
On the junior team.

352
00:21:07,271 --> 00:21:09,051
Something that Togashi said to us.

353
00:21:09,811 --> 00:21:10,331
Yeah?

354
00:21:10,331 --> 00:21:14,511
The style we've developed since junior youth is the best there is.

355
00:21:14,511 --> 00:21:16,791
I refuse to let Togashi slander it.

356
00:21:17,331 --> 00:21:20,851
But what he said that day stayed with me all these years.

357
00:21:21,671 --> 00:21:23,111
And there's a reason for that.

358
00:21:24,811 --> 00:21:29,871
Truth is, after we fought, I finally realized that I had ended up saying some pretty shitty

359
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:30,731
things to him.

360
00:21:30,731 --> 00:21:33,291
It has nothing to do with being in the academy.

361
00:21:33,851 --> 00:21:35,811
It's something I'm struggling with personally.

362
00:21:36,511 --> 00:21:40,231
If I am being weak, and I couldn't realize my weaknesses, that's on me.

363
00:21:40,451 --> 00:21:41,871
I really want to get better.

364
00:21:43,331 --> 00:21:46,911
Point is, Tachibana, I've decided to go with your strength.

365
00:21:46,911 --> 00:21:49,291
I'll stay and train some more.

366
00:21:51,931 --> 00:21:53,511
And you can count me in, too.

367
00:21:53,871 --> 00:21:56,231
I'm still on the bench, but I'm available to help.

368
00:21:57,351 --> 00:21:57,831
Really?

369
00:21:58,271 --> 00:21:59,151
Let go of me.

370
00:21:59,151 --> 00:21:59,811
Thanks, you guys.

371
00:22:06,811 --> 00:22:07,531
All right.

372
00:22:08,091 --> 00:22:08,891
Let's go!

373
00:22:09,991 --> 00:22:11,031
Be strong.

374
00:22:11,411 --> 00:22:13,651
In order to do that, I have to face my weaknesses.

375
00:22:13,651 --> 00:22:18,271
So, you're gonna pretend you've decided you want to be a pro defender now?

376
00:22:18,771 --> 00:22:22,271
How can you stand on that field without a clue as to what you're doing there?

377
00:22:24,471 --> 00:22:27,331
Do I want to be a forward or a defender?

378
00:22:29,791 --> 00:22:32,151
I'll decide for myself in the next match.

379
00:22:32,831 --> 00:22:33,991
Against Musashino!

380
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:28,706
Next time on our washing, Tokyo Metropolis League Match 8, Tokyo Musashino Football Club Youths!

